# tests/ci-manifest — CI classification for every tests/test-*.sh (XACA-0707)
#
# Format: <filename>  <category>
# Delimiter: first whitespace token (awk '{print $1}' / awk '{print $2}')
#
# Categories:
#   plain-shell    Runs via `bash tests/test-runner.sh tests/<file>` on a stock
#                  ubuntu/macos runner with no special env (beyond jq and bash
#                  installed by the test-shell-homebrew-tap job). All I/O is
#                  sandboxed under TEST_TMP_DIR; no real $HOME mutation, no
#                  network, no launchctl, no brew formula install.
#
#   brew-bash      Requires Homebrew bash 4+ (uses `declare -A` associative arrays
#                  or other bash-4-only syntax). Must be invoked as:
#                    "$(brew --prefix)/bin/bash" tests/test-runner.sh tests/<file>
#                  after `brew install bash` in the job (see XACA-0504 pattern).
#
#   real-install   Needs a real `brew install aiteamforge` formula on PATH before
#                  the test is meaningful. Belongs in the e2e-fresh-install job (or
#                  a manual post-install verification step), NOT the plain-shell job.
#
#   excluded:<reason>
#                  Must NOT be auto-run by the plain-shell runner.
#                  Reasons in use:
#                    harness-not-a-suite  — this file IS the test runner, not a suite
#                    requires-real-brew-install — manual post-install verification script
#
# Completeness gate: the CI script (tests/ci-completeness-gate.sh, XACA-0707) fails
# if any tests/test-*.sh is missing from this manifest OR if this manifest lists a
# file that no longer exists.  Add a new test-*.sh?  Add a line here first.

